[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Illusions of Pastoral Peace]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.13]Lesson 41 | 第41课
[00:02.40]Illusions of pastoral peace | 宁静田园生活的遐想
[00:10.97]What particular anxiety spoils the country dweller's visit to the theatre? | 是什么特殊的焦虑破坏了乡下人看戏的兴致？
[00:17.94]The quiet life of the country has never appealed to me. | 宁静的乡村生活从来没有吸引过我。
[00:22.45]City born and city bred, | 我生在城市，长在城市，
[00:24.90]I have always regarded the country as something you look at through a train window, or something you occasionally visit during the weekend. | 一直认为乡村是你透过火车车窗看到的某个东西，或是偶尔在周末去拜访的地方。
[00:35.61]Most of my friends live in the city, yet they always go into raptures at the mere mention of the country. | 我的大多数朋友都住在城市，然而他们一提到乡村就欣喜若狂。
[00:45.18]Though they extol the virtues of the peaceful life, | 尽管他们竭力赞美宁静生活的优点，
[00:49.15]only one of them has ever gone to live in the country and he was back in town within six months. | 其中只有一人真正去乡村生活过，而且不到6个月就又回到了城里。
[00:57.41]Even he still lives under the illusion that country life is somehow superior to town life. | 即使是他，仍然生活在乡村生活不知怎么就是优于城市生活的幻觉之中。
[01:06.07]He is forever talking about the friendly people, the clean atmosphere, the closeness to nature and the gentle pace of living. | 他喋喋不休地谈论友好的人们、洁净的空气、贴近大自然以及舒缓的生活节奏。
[01:16.04]Nothing can be compared, he maintains, with the first cockcrow, the twittering of birds at dawn, | 他坚持认为，没有什么能与清晨的第一声鸡鸣、黎明时小鸟的唧喳、
[01:24.79]the sight of the rising sun glinting on the trees and pastures. | 旭日照射在树林和牧场上闪烁的光辉相媲美。
[01:30.55]This idyllic pastoral scene is only part of the picture. | 但这田园诗般的风光只是画面的一部分。
[01:35.95]My friend fails to mention the long and friendless winter evenings in front of the TV--virtually the only form of entertainment. | 我的朋友没有提到在电视机前度过的漫长而孤独的冬夜——那几乎是唯一的娱乐形式。
[01:46.87]He says nothing about the poor selection of goods in the shops, | 他只字不提商店里商品的匮乏，
[01:51.66]or about those unfortunate people who have to travel from the country to the city every day to get to work. | 也不提那些每天不得不从乡下赶到城里上班的不幸的人们。
[02:00.73]Why people are prepared to tolerate a four-hour journey each day for the dubious privilege of living in the country is beyond me. | 为什么人们为了乡下那值得怀疑的特权，甘愿每天忍受4个小时的旅途奔波，这我无法理解。
[02:11.87]They could be saved so much misery and expense if they chose to live in the city where they rightly belong. | 如果他们选择生活在他们理应属于的城市，就可以省去许多烦恼和开支。
[02:21.99]If you can do without the few pastoral pleasures of the country, you will find the city can provide you with the best that life can offer. | 如果你可以舍弃乡村那一点点田园乐趣，你会发现城市能为你提供生活所能提供的最美好的东西。
[02:32.11]You never have to travel miles to see your friends. | 你不必走好几英里去看朋友。
[02:36.17]They invariably live nearby and are always available for an informal chat or an evening's entertainment. | 他们总住在附近，随时可以来闲聊或一起欢度夜晚。
[02:45.81]Some of my acquaintances in the country come up to town once or twice a year to visit the theatre as a special treat. | 我在乡间的一些熟人每年进城一两次，把看场戏当作特殊的享受。
[02:54.74]For them this is a major operation which involves considerable planning. | 对他们来说，这是一件需要精心筹划的大事。
[03:01.50]As the play draws to its close, they wonder whether they will ever catch that last train home. | 当戏快演完时，他们担心是否能赶上末班火车回家。
[03:08.77]The city dweller never experiences anxieties of this sort. | 城市居民从没有这种焦虑。
[03:14.16]The latest exhibitions, films, or plays are only a short bus ride away. | 最新的展览、电影或戏剧，坐一小段公共汽车就到了。
[03:21.46]Shopping, too, is always a pleasure. | 购物也总是一件乐事。
[03:25.24]There is so much variety that you never have to make do with second best. | 商品品种繁多，你从来不必将就着买二等品。
[03:32.30]Country people run wild when they go shopping in the city and stagger home loaded with as many of the exotic items as they can carry. | 乡下人进城购物时会变得疯狂，踉踉跄跄地抱回尽可能多的新奇物品。
[03:43.18]Nor is the city without its moments of beauty. | 城市也不乏美丽的时刻。
[03:47.08]There is something comforting about the warm glow shed by advertisements on cold wet winter nights. | 在寒冷潮湿的冬夜里，广告灯箱发出的暖光给人某种安慰。
[03:55.15]Few things could be more impressive than the peace that descends on deserted city streets at weekends | 很少有比周末空寂的城市街道所笼罩的宁静更令人印象深刻的东西了，
[04:02.61]when the thousands that travel to work every day are tucked away in their homes in the country. | 那时，成千上万每日进城上班的人都回到了乡下的家中。
[04:10.08]It has always been a mystery to me why city dwellers, who appreciate all these things, | 使我始终不解的是，欣赏这一切的城市居民，
[04:17.67]obstinately pretend that they would prefer to live in the country. | 却执拗地装作更愿意住在乡下。
